    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Analyze TikTok and YouTube video hooks and shot lists in Google Sheets\n\nPaste links to short videos (your own, competitors' or ads you want to learn from) and get a structured breakdown per video in a Google Sheet: the hook, format, tone, beat-by-beat structure, key moments, CTA, on-screen text and full transcript, plus views and engagement rate.\n\n### Who it's for\nUGC and performance marketers, ad buyers, agencies and creators who study what makes videos work and want a swipe file without watching every clip.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Set videos to analyze** holds TikTok, YouTube or Shorts links and the output language.\n2. **Analyze videos with Apify** sends them to the Video Breakdown AI Actor. It samples frames, reads captions (or transcribes speech with Whisper) and returns a structured analysis.\n3. **Format one row per video** turns lists into readable text cells.\n4. **Append rows to Google Sheet** adds one row per video.\n\n### Setup steps (5 min)\n1. Create an Apify account and copy your API token (Console > Settings > API & Integrations).\n2. In **Analyze videos with Apify** create a *Header Auth* credential: Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer <your token>`.\n3. Create a Google Sheet with these headers in row 1: `date, url, author, views, engagementRate, format, tone, hook, summary, structure, keyMoments, shotCount, cta, audience, onScreenText, transcript, status`. Paste its URL into **Append rows to Google Sheet** and connect Google.\n4. Replace the example links and run. Keep each run to about 10 short videos so it finishes within the 5-minute sync limit.\n\n### Customization\nSwap the manual trigger for a schedule or form, or send the hooks to an AI model to draft new scripts.\n\n*Disclosure: I maintain the Apify Actor used here.*",
        "height": 920,
        "width": 620
      },
